messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S07
Scenario title: Meeting Summary and Email Reporting
Initial workflow description:
After a meeting, the contents are summarized and shared by email with the relevant people.

Role: You coordinate clarification questions proposed by two independent questioning agents.
Task: Select and refine a complementary question set for workflow reconstruction and automation assessment.
Judge each candidate using the initial description: its relevance, the uncertainty it addresses,
the value of obtaining its answer, its likely burden on the respondent, and overlap with other candidates.
Preserve useful diverse perspectives. Do not assume any source is more authoritative.
Avoid redundant questions and bundles of unrelated information needs. You may select, rephrase,
or merge overlapping candidate questions, but cannot introduce an unrelated question.
You do not have the reference answers. Do not guess them or assume which facts an expert knows.
Candidate questions:
[
  {
    "candidate_id": "C1",
    "question": "What event or action officially signals that a meeting has ended and should trigger the summarization workflow — for example, the meeting ending in a calendar system, a manual action by the organizer, or something else?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C2",
    "question": "Who is currently responsible for producing the meeting summary — a specific role such as the meeting organizer or a designated note-taker — and is any tool or automated transcription service already involved in that step?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C3",
    "question": "How is the meeting summary currently created — is it written manually by a participant, compiled from pre-taken notes, or generated using a transcription or AI-assisted tool?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C4",
    "question": "What source material is used to create the summary — for example, live notes, an audio or video recording, an auto-generated transcript, or shared slides?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C5",
    "question": "How is the list of email recipients determined — for example, is it always the meeting attendees, a predefined distribution list, or does someone manually decide who should receive the summary?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C6",
    "question": "Is there a required format or template for the summary, such as mandatory sections for decisions made, action items with owners, or follow-up deadlines?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C7",
    "question": "Does the meeting summary need to be reviewed or approved by a specific person before the email is sent, and if so, who is responsible for that approval?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C8",
    "question": "How is the email recipient list determined after each meeting — is it fixed to all attendees, manually curated by the organizer, or driven by a rule such as role or team membership?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C9",
    "question": "Is there a required timeframe within which the summary email must be sent after the meeting concludes — such as within one hour, by end of business day, or within 24 hours?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C10",
    "question": "Does the summary need to be reviewed or approved by anyone before the email is sent, and if so, who performs that review and what is the typical turnaround time?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C11",
    "question": "Is there a standard template or set of required sections that every meeting summary must follow — such as attendees, agenda items, decisions made, and action items with owners?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C12",
    "question": "Approximately how many meetings per week trigger this summarization and email workflow, and is the volume consistent or does it vary significantly?"
  }
]
Return JSON with this shape:
{"missing_information": [{"category": "short label", "gap": "missing information", "why_it_matters": "reason"}],
"clarification_questions": [{"id": "Q1", "question": "final expert-facing question", "targets": ["short label"],
"source_ids": ["C1"], "selection_reason": "brief reason for including this question"}]}
Return exactly 6 questions with unique IDs Q1 through Q6.
Each question must have one main information need. Cite at least one valid candidate ID in source_ids.
Do not use any candidate ID for more than one final question.

